{#
# TICK-037 vendor override: this is OpenEMR 8.3.0's real, unmodified
# templates/oauth2/scope-authorize.html.twig (from PR openemr/openemr#9457/#9466,
# "granular scopes"), overridden here to fix a bug in its own reconstructScopes()
# JS: a resource with no restriction sub-categories and isUnrestricted=false was
# silently dropped from the consent POST, and multi-action resources were
# consolidated into one combined scope string (e.g. "patient/assessment.cru")
# that OpenEMR's own ResourceScopeEntityList::containsScope() can never match
# against a resource whose scopes were registered as separate single-action
# entities (any RestApiScopeEvent module scope, one addScope() call per action) --
# it checks each registered entity individually and never unions their
# permissions. Bind-mounted over the vendor path in docker-compose.yml; not a
# custom feature, just a targeted patch to an upstream defect (evidence/TICK-037).
#}
{#
# TICK-045 addition: this is also the consent screen a patient sees when the AI
# Chat portal panel's iframe (openemr_modules/aeai-portal-chat, always
# 640px-tall) needs re-authentication after the ai-server session expires. Full
# login+consent rendered inside that panel is effectively unusable (neither
# mouse-wheel scroll nor keyboard Tab reliably reached the Authorize button --
# evidence/TICK-045/CHAT_PANEL_INVESTIGATION.md, Finding 1). The `scripts` block
# below breaks the page out to a full top-level tab whenever it renders inside
# any iframe, so a patient always completes re-auth as a normal full-page flow
# instead of a form that looks stuck in a small panel. No-op when this page is
# already top-level (the common case: a direct link, or after breaking out
# once already).
#}
